"""Bombelli (1792), *Raccolta delle immagini della Beatissima Vergine ornate della corona d'oro* — transcription.

[Pietro Bombelli, incisore], *Raccolta delle immagini della Beatissima Vergine ornate della corona
d'oro dal R.mo Capitolo di S. Pietro, con una breve ed esatta notizia di ciascuna immagine*, 4 tomi
in 8°, Roma, Salomoni, 1792 (the plates of tomo IV are dated Roma 1793). One notice of four to ten
pages per image, facing an engraving by Bombelli whose caption gives the title, the support and size
of the original ("in Tavola, Alta Pal. 4, Lar. 3") and the year of the crowning. The notices draw on
"le memorie dell'archivio della Basilica Vaticana", the *memoriali* and the *atti capitolari*, and
give what no printed register gives: the DAY of the crowning, often the day of the decree, the
canons deputed, the cost of the crowns, and the separate crown for the Child.

Tomi II–IV are on the Internet Archive from the Google scans of the Biblioteca Nazionale Centrale di
Roma (bub_gb_JhP2LAUmGjUC = II, bub_gb_rHbfIRvNjxkC = III, bub_gb_9vADu01fhEAC = IV); tomo I has
not been found online. Transcribed on 14 September 2026 from the OCR text checked against the page
images wherever a date or a number was in doubt, and the caption of every plate read from the scan.
Bombelli's total is "cenquattro miracolose Imagini coronate": the 74 here in tomi II–IV, the other
thirty in tomo I. The sixteen images of the *Appendice* in tomo IV are, in his own words, "sebben non
sieno coronate", and are not transcribed.

Output: data/bombelli-1792-raccolta.json
"""
